# Testing (pytest)

Adapted from awesome-cursorrules Python testing + Gherkin-style acceptance
ideas; no Jest/Cypress.

## Conventions

- Use **pytest** only (no new unittest suites).
- Put unit tests in `tests/unit/`, integration in `tests/integration/`.
- Prefer typed fixtures; keep fixtures tiny and synthetic under
  `tests/fixtures/`.
- Cover permutation invariance, missing-gene / presence mask, path policy, and
  schema/manifest validation where those modules change.
- Mark slow tests; default agent checks:
  `uv run pytest tests/unit` and
  `uv run pytest tests/integration -m "not slow"`.

## Acceptance wording

When defining or verifying milestone **Done when** criteria, write them as
observable outcomes (artifact path, schema-valid manifest, test name)—not
"code exists".
